From 72c602c626c17da1505b108fc699a054b1804879 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 13:17:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ci(boru): the job dies of SIGPIPE, not of a broken build

omni's boru job has failed on every run since it was added. It fails at
"Build the boru CLI", which reads as though the CLI will not build. It builds
fine: the log prints the help line and then exits 141, and 141 is 128+13 -
SIGPIPE.

`head -1` exits after one line and closes the pipe while `boru help` is still
writing; `set -o pipefail` promotes that to a step failure. `sed -n '1p'`
drains its input instead, and pipefail still catches a genuine failure of the
CLI.

The `BORU=$RUNNER_TEMP/boru` on the next line is quoted at the same time:
unquoted it is shellcheck SC2086, which actionlint reports in repos that run
it - voxgig/struct does, and flagged the identical line in its copy of this
job.

Both defects are the same two voxgig/struct hit, because this job was modelled
on struct's. Fixed there in main@8198652.
---
 .github/workflows/ci.yml | 14 ++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/.github/workflows/ci.yml b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
index f2a0e9a..9071a67 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/ci.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
@@ -335,8 +335,18 @@ jobs:
           set -euo pipefail
           cd "$GITHUB_WORKSPACE/.boru-lang/cmd/go"
           go build -o "$RUNNER_TEMP/boru" ./boru
-          "$RUNNER_TEMP/boru" help | head -1
-      - run: make test-boru BORU=$RUNNER_TEMP/boru
+          # `sed -n 1p`, NOT `head -1`: head exits after the first line and
+          # closes the pipe, so `boru help` dies of SIGPIPE writing the rest -
+          # exit 141, which the `set -o pipefail` above promotes to a step
+          # failure even though the build and the CLI are both fine. Measured:
+          # that is exactly how this job failed on its first run here, and in
+          # voxgig/struct's copy of it before that. sed drains its input, so
+          # there is nothing to signal, and pipefail still catches a genuine
+          # failure of the CLI. Do not add `;q` to the sed script.
+          "$RUNNER_TEMP/boru" help | sed -n '1p'
+      # Quoted: unquoted this is shellcheck SC2086, which actionlint reports
+      # in repos that run it (voxgig/struct does, and flagged the twin).
+      - run: make test-boru BORU="$RUNNER_TEMP/boru"
 
   struct-compat:
     name: struct compatibility
-- 
2.43.0

